data.content:
No, implementation can't safely start from this specification. Two of its checks would let a wrong behaviour through.

```yaml
verdict: NEEDS_REWORK
confidence: medium
lenses:
  coverage:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "Gold example expects 8400 cents; AC-3 says 8500 cents. The wrong value would pin a 16% discount instead of 15%.", location: "discount.feature:16"}
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "AC-4 (Bronze, 7 cents, whole-cent rounding) has no scenario. The test plan matrix stops at AC-3 yet claims every criterion is covered.", location: "discount.feature"}
      - {gate: G2, severity: HIGH, finding: "No boundary or rounding case is present. Every example uses 10000 cents, where each percentage divides exactly, so a wrong rounding rule would pass.", location: "discount.feature:13-16"}
      - {gate: G1, severity: MEDIUM, finding: "AC-4 contradicts itself. 5% of 7 cents leaves 6.65, so 'in the customer's favour' means 6 cents, but the AC says 7. Settle it with the story owner.", location: "ac.md:19-22"}
  business-alignment: {status: pass, findings: []}
  testability:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: T3, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "No production skeleton exists (CalculateLoyaltyDiscount, query, LoyaltyTier, quote). The outer test fails to compile instead of failing on a business assertion.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:14-18"}
      - {gate: G9, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "The acceptance test copies the wrong Gold value (8400), so it would lock the bug in. It also has no AC-4 case.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:11"}
      - {gate: G6, severity: HIGH, finding: "The implementation plan has no per-scenario entry, file paths or use case boundary.", location: "impl.md"}
      - {gate: G11, severity: LOW, finding: "The Application test is in the UnitTest project, so the gate passes. The impl plan does not reference the file.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:6"}
  boundary-enforcement:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G7, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "No contracts file exists, so CalculateLoyaltyDiscount.Handle cannot be checked. The matrix has no AC-4 row.", location: "test.md:6-10"}
      - {gate: G8, severity: HIGH, finding: "No walking skeleton scenario is identified in the plan.", location: "test.md"}
synthesis:
  questions:
    completeness: {answered_by: [coverage], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.00}
    business-fit: {answered_by: [business-alignment], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.30}
    quality: {answered_by: [testability], weight: 0.15, contribution: 0.00}
    risk: {answered_by: [boundary-enforcement], weight: 0.25, contribution: 0.00}
  blocking_findings:
    - "G1: Gold 8400 in the feature file against 8500 in AC-3"
    - "G1: AC-4 has no scenario, and the test plan claims full coverage"
    - "T3: no production skeleton, so the outer test cannot reach a business-assertion RED"
    - "G9: the acceptance test repeats the wrong Gold value of 8400"
    - "G7: the contracts file is missing"
  recommendations:
    - "Correct Gold to 8500 in the feature file and the test."
    - "Resolve the AC-4 expected value (6 or 7 cents), then add a scenario, a matrix row and a test case."
    - "Add the skeleton production files, each returning the empty value of its type."
    - "Write contracts, a per-scenario impl plan with paths, and a walking skeleton marker."
  dissent: "Business-alignment passes: the Gherkin wording is clean. It is not overridden, but it does not offset the blockers in the other three lenses."
```

**What would let a wrong behaviour through:**
- **Gold value:** the feature file and the test both expect 8400 cents, but AC-3 says 8500. Implementing to the test would give Gold a 16% discount.
- **Rounding:** AC-4 has no scenario or test. Every example uses 10000 cents, which divides exactly, so any rounding rule would pass.
- **AC-4 itself:** it says a 7-cent basket is charged 7 cents, but 5% off 7 cents is 6.65. Rounding in the customer's favour would charge 6. That needs a decision from the story owner.

The verdict is saved to `.copilot-tracking/skraft-plans/pricing/reviews/2026-10-18/distill-review-1.md`. I did not edit any reviewed artefact.
